# Project Testing Phase - Implement Client Script & UI Policy for Incident

## 1. Testing Objective
To verify that Client Scripts and UI Policies work correctly on Incident form without conflicts.

## 2. Test Cases

### Test Case 1: onLoad Script
- Action: Open an existing Incident with Priority = 1
- Expected: Info message "This is a Critical Priority Incident!" should appear
- Result: Pass

### Test Case 2: onChange Script
- Action: Enter Short Description less than 10 characters
- Expected: Error message "Short description must be at least 10 characters"
- Result: Pass

### Test Case 3: onSubmit Script
- Action: Try to submit Incident without Category
- Expected: Form should not submit and show error "Category is mandatory"
- Result: Pass

### Test Case 4: UI Policy - Software Category
- Action: Select Category = Software
- Expected: Software field should become visible and mandatory
- Result: Pass

### Test Case 5: UI Policy - Hardware Category
- Action: Select Category = Hardware
- Expected: Hardware related fields should become visible
- Result: Pass

## 3. Bug Fixes
- Fixed Client Script not triggering by checking Active checkbox
- Fixed UI Policy not working by setting correct reverse conditions

## 4. Final Validation
- All Client Scripts working as expected
- All UI Policies working without conflict
- No console errors

## 5. Conclusion
Testing completed successfully. Implementation is ready for final submission.
